# The build context for this image is the AgentDrive root, and Docker reads
# ONLY the `.dockerignore` at the context root — so this file is the one that
# applies to the AgentDrive image, whatever repository holds it.
#
# There used to be a file here and it was DELETED when the port moved the
# build to a repo-root context, precisely because it had become inert and
# would have read as load-bearing while doing nothing. The context moved back
# inside the app so that a checkout of AgentDrive alone can build the image
# (open-source design §4.4), which brings the file back with it. Its rules are
# the app-relevant subset of the root file's, restated rather than referenced:
# an ignore file cannot include another one.
.git

# Node build output and installs. `mcp/{auth,server}/dist` in particular must
# never enter the context: the image builds the sidecar from `src` with its
# own pinned manifests, and a stale `dist` from a developer's laptop landing
# in the layer cache is a build that ships something nobody reviewed.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next

# Local secret material and generated cloud credentials must never enter a
# build context, even when an auth action creates them in the tree. The list
# is this app's OWN `.gitignore` read as a threat model rather than as a
# convenience: anything it keeps out of the repository because it is private
# has the same reason to stay out of a build context, and `docker build` from
# a working tree is exactly where the two lists diverge.
.env*
!.env.example
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
gha-creds-*.json
**/gha-creds-*.json
**/.pgpass
**/application_default_credentials.json
*.key
**/*.key
*.pem
**/*.pem
deploy/.deployrc
docker-compose.override.yml
.worktrees
.superpowers

# The filesystem object store a local `STORAGE_BACKEND=fs` run writes into.
# Not secret, but unbounded: every `docker build` would otherwise hand the
# daemon whatever a developer has uploaded.
var

# Coverage artifacts. Local tooling, and `htmlcov/` is thousands of files.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
coverage.xml

# Terraform downloads, state, variable values and saved plans are local
# operator artifacts, not image inputs. This app owns its own Terraform tree
# (`infra/terraform`, one state file per product), so the exclusion has to be
# here as well as at the root.
infra/terraform
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfplan
**/terraform.tfvars
**/*.auto.tfvars
**/*.auto.tfvars.json

# Python build/venv/cache artifacts. Without these, `COPY src` ships every
# `__pycache__` inside it.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/*.egg-info

# The legacy black-box harness. It needs its own `.env.e2e` (covered above)
# and is never part of an image. The `archive/` and `.ai/` rules that stood
# here were removed unread: neither directory exists any more, and this file's
# own header argues against carrying a rule that does nothing.
tests/e2e
